jobs.description:
We do have a few wishes before we can offer you this job:
-- You will need to have a C driving license with code 95;
-- You speak and understand Dutch or English well;  
-- You are customer-friendly, flexible and solution-oriented;     
-- You handle fresh food products with care.           

NICE VACANCY FOR A TRUCK DRIVER 

-- EARN MONEY WHILE DRIVING THROUGH THE NETHERLANDS?
-- Yes, that will be possible soon!

-- At a renowned fresh food and catering company, you can pick up the most tasteful culinary dishes and deliver them to various hotels, restaurants, healthcare institutions or simply to festivals and private parties!

-- You travel a lot and therefore work many hours, for which you get paid!
& every day fresh and healthy snacks are ready for you on the go! 

-- We offer you:
-- A good working atmosphere with motivated and experienced colleagues;
-- A comfortable truck;
-- Excellent primary and secondary employment conditions, in accordance with the collective labor agreement;
-- Development opportunities and training.
-------- If you are interested, please let us know!

Your shift starts with a team briefing, where you and your colleagues discuss the day's workload and priorities. Once everything is clear, you begin processing goods and customer orders in the warehouse.

Your responsibilities include:

• Checking incoming goods;
• Picking orders using a scanner;
• Packing customer orders;
• Repacking returned orders so they are ready for shipment again;
• Processing incoming and outgoing goods;
• Performing light administrative tasks when required;
• Keeping the warehouse clean and organized together with your team at the end of the shift.

Functie-eisen:
This role is suitable for someone who enjoys working accurately and efficiently in a warehouse environment.

Requirements:

• You work accurately and are comfortable rolling up your sleeves;
• You speak fluent Dutch or English;
• You are available for evening shifts (13:00 - 21:30 or 14:30 - 23:00);
• You are occasionally available on weekends;
• You have good computer skills;
• You can quickly learn light administrative tasks.

We are looking for a Logistics Reception & Expedition Employee for our logistics department. In this versatile role, you will be the first point of contact for drivers and ensure that incoming and outgoing goods flow smoothly and correctly.

- Receiving and registering drivers and visitors;
- Coordinating incoming and outgoing goods;
- Checking freight documents and transport documentation;
- Administrative processing in the logistics system;
- Managing loading and unloading processes;
- Assisting with loading and unloading;
- Ensuring order, cleanliness, and safety in the dispatch area.

- Experience in a logistics role;
- Experience with an EPT, forklift, or reach truck;
- Good communication skills;
- Accurate and stress-resistant work ethic;
- Basic knowledge of MS Office and logistics systems;
- You speak the English language.
